      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The modern approach to harm prevention often leads to a gray area when it comes to high-profile figures or provocative commentary. While social media platforms have taken steps to protect users from targeted harassment, they also risk infringing on free speech when moderating high-profile accounts. In such cases, courts and advocacy groups often favor a balancing act that strikes a delicate trade-off between protecting sensitive groups and preserving free expression. Ultimately, platforms face scrutiny if their policies unfairly suppress specific viewpoints or ideologies.",
